## Initial Q&A
### Did New Zealand's Parliament pass an Abortion Legislation Act in 2020?
Answer: Yes, New Zealand's Parliament passed an abortion reform bill in 2020. According to the BBC article, "New Zealand's parliament has passed a bill decriminalising abortion and allowing women to choose a termination up to 20weeks into a pregnancy," with the bill passing on its third reading by 68 votes to 51.

Source URL: https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-51955148

### Does New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 permit abortions after 20 weeks of gestation?
Answer: Yes, New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 does permit abortions after 20 weeks of gestation, but with conditions. According to the source, "abortion is available without restrictions to any woman who is not more than 20 weeks pregnant," and "Women seeking an abortion after 20 weeks have to be looked at by a qualified health professional." This means that while abortions after 20 weeks are not outright banned, they require assessment by a qualified health professional rather than being available on request.

Source URL: https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abortion_Legislation_Act_2020

### Does New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 permit abortions during the third trimester of pregnancy?
Answer: Based on the search result, the source does not explicitly address whether third-trimester abortions are permitted under the Act. It only states that "There are no statutory requirements for abortions up to 20 weeks of pregnancy" and that "Multi-disciplinary care is necessary for women who have pregnancies over 20 weeks," but it does not specify whether abortions in the third trimester (typically 28+ weeks) are allowed or prohibited.

Source URL: https://www.midwife.org.nz/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/Abortion-Act-summary_JUNE2020.pdf

### Does New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 permit abortions up to the point of birth?
Answer: No. According to the source, under the Abortion Legislation Act 2020, "abortion is available without restrictions to any woman who is not more than 20 weeks pregnant," and "Women seeking an abortion after 20 weeks have to be looked at by a qualified health professional." This means abortions after 20 weeks are not freely available and require medical consultation, so the Act does not permit abortions up to the point of birth without restriction.

Source URL: https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abortion_Legislation_Act_2020

### Does New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 permit sex-selective abortions?
Answer: The search result does not specifically address sex-selective abortions. It describes the general framework of the Act—abortion available on request up to 20 weeks, and after 20 weeks if a health practitioner "reasonably believes that the abortion is clinically appropriate in the circumstances"—but does not mention any specific prohibition on sex-selective abortions.

