### What abortion methods were legally available in New Zealand immediately before the 2020 Abortion Legislation Act was passed?
Answer: Immediately before the 2020 Abortion Legislation Act was passed, two main abortion methods were legally available in New Zealand under the Crimes Act 1961 and the Contraception, Sterilisation,and Abortion Act 1977: **surgical abortion**, with "dilation and suction curettage" being "the most common method of abortion in the first trimester," and **medical abortion** using the abortion pill mifepristone (RU486), introduced in 2002, in which "mifepristone and prostaglandin were used in approximately three-quarters of medical abortions carried out in the first nine weeks of pregnancy." However, access to these services varied by region, and both methods required approval by two medical consultants.

Source URL: https://teara.govt.nz/en/abortion/page-5

## Final Judgement
