The evidence confirms that New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 was passed and allows abortion on request up to 20 weeks, with abortions after 20 weeks permitted subject to assessment by a qualified health professional. The Act does not permit unrestricted abortions up to the point of birth. Regarding the specific claim about "controversial abortion methods," the only source addressing this is Right To Life UK itself (the claim author), which asserts that "there will be no legal restrictions on controversial methods of abortion such as intact dilation and extraction abortions." However, this source does not cite the specific statutory text, and no independent or neutral legal analysis was retrieved to verify which specific methods are permitted or prohibited under the Act.

